From: G98 LEDE maintainers <lede@bdy-g98.local>
Date: Mon, 24 Aug 2026 20:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] phy: rockchip: usbdp: propagate clock lookup errors

devm_clk_bulk_get_all() may return -EPROBE_DEFER while the USB2 PHY
clock provider is still probing. Converting every non-positive return
value to -ENODEV prevents the USBDP PHY from being retried and leaves
its DWC3 consumer permanently deferred.

Propagate clock lookup errors and handle an empty clock list
separately so the driver core can retry the probe.

Signed-off-by: G98 LEDE maintainers <lede@bdy-g98.local>
---
 drivers/phy/rockchip/phy-rockchip-usbdp.c | 7 +++++--
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/phy/rockchip/phy-rockchip-usbdp.c
+++ b/drivers/phy/rockchip/phy-rockchip-usbdp.c
@@ -427,8 +427,11 @@ static int rk_udphy_clk_init(struct rk_u
 	int i;
 
 	udphy->num_clks = devm_clk_bulk_get_all(dev, &udphy->clks);
-	if (udphy->num_clks < 1)
-		return -ENODEV;
+	if (udphy->num_clks < 0)
+		return dev_err_probe(dev, udphy->num_clks,
+				     "failed to get clocks\n");
+	if (!udphy->num_clks)
+		return dev_err_probe(dev, -ENODEV, "no clocks found\n");
 
 	/* used for configure phy reference clock frequency */
 	for (i = 0; i < udphy->num_clks; i++) {
